 /* end--演示页面使用的统一样式--end */
+
+/* OFFLINE ADAPTATION (repair-bench) - vendor runtime preload neutralised.
+   The @dcloudio/uni-h5 runtime stylesheet ships, verbatim in the built bundle
+   (measured: dist/build/h5/assets/index-iCk2Ehn7.css),
+     body:after{position:fixed;content:"";left:-1000px;top:-1000px;
+                animation:shadow-preload .1s;animation-delay:3s}
+     @keyframes shadow-preload{0%{background-image:url(https://cdn.dcloud.net.cn/img/shadow-grey.png)}
+                              to{background-image:url(https://cdn.dcloud.net.cn/...)}}
+   i.e. an off-screen pseudo-element that preloads a remote image 3 SECONDS after every page load. That
+   is exactly the second blocked host the gate-1 probe saw (cdn.dcloud.net.cn, 2 requests = the two
+   keyframe stops) and it is NOT in src/ at all (rg over src/ + index.html: 0 hits), so it cannot be
+   fixed at its own source and must not be fixed inside node_modules (the delivered recipe restores
+   node_modules from the durable nm archive, which no patch may touch). This file is @import-ed LAST in
+   the global <style> block of src/App.vue (line 19), and the override is !important so bundle order is
+   irrelevant. Killing the animation means the keyframes never apply, so neither URL is ever requested.
+   Nothing observable changes: body:after is an invisible off-screen preload hack at (-1000px,-1000px). */
+body::after {
+    animation: none !important;
+    background-image: none !important;
+}
